=== Surface summary (P3 acceptance evidence) ===
- Gate result: BUILD_EXIT=0 (:android:assembleRelease), TEST_EXIT=0 (:android:testReleaseUnitTest, full suite),
  LINT_EXIT=0 (:android:ktlintCheck over every source set + :android:detekt), PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0 / PLACEHOLDER_EXIT=0.
- Module path: the prompt gate's :app: project does not exist; settings.gradle.kts maps :android -> app/. The real
  :android: tasks were run (the sibling ConfirmDialog / AddAnnotationPopover surfaces gate the same way).
- Surface shape: GeofenceDrawer is the native port of web/src/components/maps/GeofenceDrawer.tsx -- a leaflet-draw
  controller mounted on the parent map. Its only web "hook" is useMap (the map context); it binds NO S8 data store
  and makes NO HTTP call. A finished draft / a deletion are handed to the parent via onCreate(DraftGeofence) /
  onDelete(id), exactly like the web onCreate / onDelete props. Because the source has no cache-then-network
  lifecycle, the prompt's generic loading/empty/error/stale/offline DATA states do not exist in the source and are
  NOT fabricated (that would be drift). The states the source actually has are all reproduced, no hidden surfaces:
    * rendered shapes -> the existing fences drawn as circles / areas on the map; GeofenceDrawerProjection
      .renderableFences applies the web fenceToLayer-returns-null guard (a circle needs radius > 0; an area needs
      >= 3 vertices) so an unrenderable fence is never handed to the editor as a silent no-op.
    * draw toolbar -> circle by default (web modes=['circle'], the only shape GeofencesPage enables and persists);
      tap-to-place draft + radius slider; Save enables only once the draft is complete.
    * accessible list -> one labelled row per fence with a per-row delete (the web describeFence non-visual
      alternative), reusing the shared describeGeofence wording.
    * no-fences branch -> the editor + localized hint still render (a friendly editor, never a blank box).
    * dismiss -> the shared Modal scrim / system-back / close button (onDismiss).
- Tier adaptation (declared, not silent): the web component mounts inline on <MapContainer> and renders no chrome of
  its own. The P3 tier classifies this artifact as a modal/dialog surface ("focus trap + dismiss semantics"), so the
  native host wraps the SAME editor in the shared Modal shell and gates it on an `open` flag -- the Compose idiom for
  the web `open` prop the sibling AddAnnotationPopover uses. The on-map shapes + draw toolbar + accessible list are
  the real, working atomic editor (io.teslasync.android.components.maps.GeofenceDrawer, the P3 component-library
  bundle -- OUT OF SCOPE here), reused rather than reimplemented and driven entirely through its i18n-resolved label
  parameters.
- i18n (P1/S10): every Kotlin string resolves via stringResource from the EXISTING generated catalog -- no new keys,
  no English literals in shipped .kt. Keys used: translation_geofences_drawOnMap (modal title + draw affordance),
  translation_geofences_drawHint, translation_geofences_drawerLabel (map content description),
  translation_geofences_aiSuggest_radiusLabel, translation_Geofences (list header), translation_common_close /
  _clear / _save / _delete. The web source extracts NO i18n keys (its toolbar uses leaflet-draw's own bundled
  control tooltips, not our catalog), so there is no shape-name key to match; the surface is circle-only by default
  and routes each shape's draw affordance through geofences.drawOnMap.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): one-shot PII-safe view.opened emitted with surface slug "GeofenceDrawer" (carries no fence
  name, coordinate, or radius) from the composable's first-composition LaunchedEffect.
- Tests: GeofenceDrawerModelTest (off-device adapter / per-branch / diagnostics coverage -- renderable-fence filter,
  order preservation, hasFences, summaryLines, DEFAULT_MODES, registry ids, the view.opened diagnostic -- executed
  by the testReleaseUnitTest step above) + GeofenceDrawerUiTest (instrumented a11y/UI: toolbar contentDescriptions,
  the accessible map label, the list header, the per-row delete hand-off, the no-fences branch). The UI test runs
  under connectedAndroidTest on a device/emulator -- not part of this offline gate; it passed
  :android:ktlintAndroidTestSourceSetCheck.
- androidTest note: compiling the whole androidTest source set (:android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin) fails on
  PRE-EXISTING, unrelated errors in sibling files (Unresolved reference assertExists / assertDoesNotExist in
  FSMStateDiagramUiTest + several dashboard-widget + featureviews tests) that are OUTSIDE this surface's allowed
  files and OUTSIDE this gate. This surface's own GeofenceDrawerUiTest uses none of those APIs and is not in the
  error set; it is ktlint-clean.
- Files beyond the templated allow-list: the two test files (acceptance #5 requires adapter + per-state UI + a11y
